@*
    Task 7.3: this is Views/Widget/WidgetsByZone.cshtml, relocated to the location ASP.NET Core
    searches for a view component's default view.

    A view component renders "Components/{ComponentName}/{ViewName}", so
    Nop.Web.Framework.Themes.ThemeableViewLocationExpander resolves this file through its
    existing "/Views/Shared/{0}.cshtml" format - which also means a theme can still override it
    at /Themes/{theme}/Views/Shared/Components/Widget/Default.cshtml. Hardcoding the old path
    with View("~/Views/Widget/WidgetsByZone.cshtml") would have compiled and rendered, but would
    have bypassed the expander and silently made this partial un-themeable.

    The body is unchanged. Html.Action here is the DYNAMIC case that makes the child-action
    bridge unavoidable: the controller and action names come from IWidgetPlugin at runtime, so
    they cannot be expressed as a view component. See Nop.Web/Extensions/ChildActionExtensions.cs.
*@
@model List<RenderWidgetModel>
@using Nop.Web.Models.Cms;
@foreach (var widget in Model)
{
    @Html.Action(widget.ActionName, widget.ControllerName, widget.RouteValues)
}
